[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186150041 :answer-field/choices 17592186150046] {:db/id 17592186152178 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151973 :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $U.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $U$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. So, $U$ is a local maximum.\n\nA similar interval exists for the point $W,$ too. So, $W$ is also a local maximum.\n\n![](images/ac/ac0a6e28e4564883e6743b2d600cb8611723e813e85c1acb5fcc327ee3dbc9b5.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152216 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" "question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" "question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152026 :question/problem "For which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y = f(x),$ shown below, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=0$\n\nII. $x=1$\n\nIII. $x=3$\n\n![](images/17/1718b48d39255b221037a439cc48d300a04c33ffb4e04c700fefb303a20ebff2.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=0.$ For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/e2/e25e6e31d6ea5d7f882d4eed16c82ec8280d1ed56f275974e8f07091c0e62c5d.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(0) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-0.5,0.5).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=1.$ For any open interval containing $x=1$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(1)$.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/d1/d133d7ee4c022b47740f62b8e73ba9ea2f70e788861c25d2824b5e7236027c60.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(3) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152217 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" "question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152027 :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the function shown below. Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=-2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=0$\n\n![](images/9b/9b933b1b869b74f2a7340f9ba4034b970c49434d12592d3ff1e152057b6adef1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/3a/3abb7470db51fa1bdb61e15aec1739de44bf5083b7341b90a65ac93fc7f8adbb.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(-2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/71/71c6e7af0a1de77543b57d2aee242fe84295ad46c748b2f65f7cba381c47b80c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=0.$ For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/83/83de300c3e00766d46989d12b4e1708ef9a73f4d02748009a526b1646d7f0b81.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\le f(0) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-0.5,0.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152218 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" "question-f8983cc1-bd12-59ce-89e8-0458cbfae2b2" "question-f3f7c8b0-18ee-5d7c-bcd5-63f6de1aef9a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152028 :question/problem "The graph of a function $y = f(x)$ is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=0$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-2$\n\n![](images/91/91d9d4997dd58c2c3cb07efc1529487bbd9a5a2f5c611054289cfc2ba24d764c.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/00/00a21a670b2080ce766ddf142eb2f37303d7af7b667e1b5038eee93879c071f7.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function does *not* have a global maximum at $x=0.$ The global maximum is the highest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is greater than $f(0).$ For example, $f(0) \\lt f(3).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/fc/fc96fe5bb938b0ca8569b864588348a4d22280e3c4a5806cdd20af6eb4bcea34.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(-2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152589 :question/problem "![](images/20/20b6e19fcb7e1fe4f33697d517c28d9563c793634cfbcd5552d842efeef3ef61.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $B.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $B$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. Hence, $B$ is a local maximum.\n\nA similar interval exists for the point $D,$ too. Hence, $D$ is also a local maximum.\n\n![](images/26/260f30379f71c006b43ec6eb26200ced27a4b40aec938140d6a4cd06910ba02c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186150041 :answer-field/correct 17592186150042 :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854" :answer/id #uuid "d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A,$ $C,$ and $E$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/id #uuid "2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-37221" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbe19cf01b4ca415802db1d505b402e2c238aad6c443170cf18cd7b79d7f238a.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $Q.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $Q$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. Hence, $Q$ is a local maximum.\n\n![](images/14/14d2e4c17f5a79165c2e6b1988fe949625eccb87d2880b1131705028be5884c4.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121" "answer-69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3" "answer-a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a" "answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" "answer-abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121" :answer/id #uuid "36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3" :answer/id #uuid "69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a" :answer/id #uuid "a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" :answer/id #uuid "a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330" :answer/id #uuid "abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function does not have local maxima" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/id #uuid "2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-37056" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d65013cac950b3e3d533dd6dfbdf1dc6582c10fcb7d80f00ab559935915d9595.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local maximum?\n\nI. $x=-1$\n\nII. $x=1$\n\nIII. $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local maximum at $x=-1.$ For example, in the interval $(-1.25,-0.75),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=-1,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/a5/a5f0e23d8bed98f693ee72086b0bf17b9f65de8931bba6f16cfcc34e670a757e.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(-1)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-1.25,-0.75).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local maximum at $x=1.$ For any open interval containing $x=1,$ there will be points on the graph that lie above $f(1).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local maximum at $x=3.$ For any open interval containing $x=3,$ there will be points on the graph that lie above $f(3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/id #uuid "90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223" "answer-959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8" "answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" "answer-78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02" "answer-1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223" :answer/id #uuid "e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8" :answer/id #uuid "959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" :answer/id #uuid "ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02" :answer/id #uuid "78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad" :answer/id #uuid "1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/id #uuid "95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-108276" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d71ebdb084e23aef4b3901aaba2e4bb4de5438fa41a3fc331bef749f3c78de76.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=-4$\n\nII. $x=-1$\n\nIII. $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=-4.$ For any open interval containing $x=-4$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(-4).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=-1.$ For any open interval containing $x=-1$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(-1).$\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/bf/bfe274fe02b7200164eaad5c98aa2b19297738987f70059157d2895b989a962c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/id #uuid "73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd" "answer-274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480" "answer-6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224" "answer-4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434" "answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd" :answer/id #uuid "0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480" :answer/id #uuid "274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224" :answer/id #uuid "6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434" :answer/id #uuid "4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a" :answer/id #uuid "8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152594 :question/problem "![](images/c4/c46e88b9e044fccb91e0efa4ee981973a286e0335f58a70f7b1f9a856d9bfed4.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=3$\n\nII. $x=2$\n\nIII. $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.75,3.25),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/61/6115a87572fb93b9e3dcf69c75cd4a5efaae2dbbea90b28cb57cdd05b8db11b7.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.75,3.25).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=2.$ For any open interval containing $x=2$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(2).$\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/26/26acee415fa4a1038077d11f88b7c61c8b45f4aa857cc578af192e4085f7c005.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186150071 :answer-field/correct 17592186150075 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/id #uuid "ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-108273" :question/problem "![](images/69/69217ab9fc86fdbb424a0716f00596197b7da9e930c74b12b82406ce2ee8354c.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=-2$\n\nII. $x=2$\n\nIII. $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For any open interval containing $x=-2,$ there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(-2).$\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/8e/8e56e79caf5c7903de977ee66894961b6068e3974ffd9ff4482b2086fad290ef.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=4.$ For any open interval containing $x=4,$ there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(4).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66" "answer-d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2" "answer-02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2" "answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" "answer-2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66" :answer/id #uuid "2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2" :answer/id #uuid "d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2" :answer/id #uuid "02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" :answer/id #uuid "5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97" :answer/id #uuid "2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/id #uuid "a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/math-academy-id "q-108281" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b39c4e174ccb11a533586b57f26958a8ebfb5de0f0920a86297653471862fa7f.png)\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the function shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-3$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=0$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-3.$ For example, in the interval $(-3.5,-2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/be/be3b86690beb961d54380b72736d945af3d735410da3bfe34cfb2cdead859f81.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(-3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-3.5,-2.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=0.$ For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/43/439117bd94dbc147d3cd2de49abd45c4b4790251ce25d1a79ecb31e03081068c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(0)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-0.5,0.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.75,3.25),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/33/33aee4724507cff3e9ca87c78aa77c0ecb0df5f59a7bcf77359c1ca4e957f73c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(3)\\le f(x)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.75,3.25).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" "answer-caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548" "answer-fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce" "answer-527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358" "answer-2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" :answer/id #uuid "601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548" :answer/id #uuid "caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce" :answer/id #uuid "fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358" :answer/id #uuid "527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3" :answer/id #uuid "2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/id #uuid "50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-108293" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b00882caec033394ff22a01df1f8cc417a8336b475962e73662316c3091229fa.png)\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the function given by the graph above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=-2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/ed/ed1ad21056cf9c05c621180126387f2e07a1cd349f151726142fb33d2b514e44.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(-2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1.$ For example, in the interval $(0.5,1.5),$ the value of the function at $x=1$ is the same as the values of the function at the other points of the interval, as shown below. \n\n![](images/ff/ff8960289497889b1fb046c05b0bb2243a8776c435bb685e3c94fb7fe832e056.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(1)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (0.5,1.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local maximum at $x=4.$ For example, in the interval $(3.75,4.25),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/b2/b2d1f1b6b065c5d3511ec02350eae1a867b9473fa2ac7c1a1cb9458d1421fe03.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(4)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (3.75,4.25).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/id #uuid "a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" :answer-field/choices ["answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" "answer-2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8" "answer-b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6" "answer-e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487" "answer-3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" :answer/id #uuid "813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8" :answer/id #uuid "2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6" :answer/id #uuid "b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487" :answer/id #uuid "e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b" :answer/id #uuid "3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/id #uuid "e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/math-academy-id "q-90634" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d13474a62324af5edcaafd10e60c6b02c257f32c015d5769512725d157e01420.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=4$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** minimum at $x=5$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function does *not* have a global maximum at $x=4.$ The global maximum is the highest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is greater than $f(4).$ For example, $f(7)>f(4).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/32/32c866706140c0bc9a40bcb0ffdca4a827578e2d16dbcefc2cdb66b5c05b1c1c.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function does *not* have a global minimum at $x=5.$ The global minimum is the lowest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is smaller than $f(5).$ For example, $f(0)<f(5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cf7eaa68-885c-514e-a7ed-820109c92b1a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cf7eaa68-885c-514e-a7ed-820109c92b1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7eaa68-885c-514e-a7ed-820109c92b1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7d044135-ffc0-53de-a8ed-edcab8fbf246" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08" "answer-7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98" "answer-79e94892-8258-5ef2-824f-178abd4ba976" "answer-8bc7c11b-5e49-5add-a829-e5b05338f3ea" "answer-7d044135-ffc0-53de-a8ed-edcab8fbf246"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08" :answer/id #uuid "f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98" :answer/id #uuid "7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79e94892-8258-5ef2-824f-178abd4ba976" :answer/id #uuid "79e94892-8258-5ef2-824f-178abd4ba976" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bc7c11b-5e49-5add-a829-e5b05338f3ea" :answer/id #uuid "8bc7c11b-5e49-5add-a829-e5b05338f3ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d044135-ffc0-53de-a8ed-edcab8fbf246" :answer/id #uuid "7d044135-ffc0-53de-a8ed-edcab8fbf246" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8983cc1-bd12-59ce-89e8-0458cbfae2b2" :question/id #uuid "f8983cc1-bd12-59ce-89e8-0458cbfae2b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-90637" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e0125007c4384cdd3eb5d939176b2d1ede7a6525da26fb5e99ccfe67e4077a9.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=4$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=3$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function has a global maximum at $x=4.$ The global maximum is the highest point on the graph and our function does *not* have points where its value is greater than $f(4).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/c2/c288ece1ca29e5da8ec8d64583b25f7538a929a3de295c24be6396339649d2d4.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function does *not* have a global maximum at $x=1.$ The global maximum is the highest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is greatest than $f(1).$ For example, $f(4)>f(1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-50bdcfb3-d31d-58ba-ade3-e108e9937b5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-50bdcfb3-d31d-58ba-ade3-e108e9937b5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "50bdcfb3-d31d-58ba-ade3-e108e9937b5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-69d3c833-109c-55b6-b9de-758ec5a86527" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69d3c833-109c-55b6-b9de-758ec5a86527" "answer-92c3e3d1-b0c8-562f-8bcd-8d77d551c467" "answer-a79e3ac5-259e-5485-aea5-ad1f8c55e3cd" "answer-a6c18fdc-de58-518a-8778-1344568ab9bb" "answer-0f56b3cc-115f-57ad-a4f5-2b4f7ee5bbfb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69d3c833-109c-55b6-b9de-758ec5a86527" :answer/id #uuid "69d3c833-109c-55b6-b9de-758ec5a86527" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92c3e3d1-b0c8-562f-8bcd-8d77d551c467" :answer/id #uuid "92c3e3d1-b0c8-562f-8bcd-8d77d551c467" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a79e3ac5-259e-5485-aea5-ad1f8c55e3cd" :answer/id #uuid "a79e3ac5-259e-5485-aea5-ad1f8c55e3cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6c18fdc-de58-518a-8778-1344568ab9bb" :answer/id #uuid "a6c18fdc-de58-518a-8778-1344568ab9bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f56b3cc-115f-57ad-a4f5-2b4f7ee5bbfb" :answer/id #uuid "0f56b3cc-115f-57ad-a4f5-2b4f7ee5bbfb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3f7c8b0-18ee-5d7c-bcd5-63f6de1aef9a" :question/id #uuid "f3f7c8b0-18ee-5d7c-bcd5-63f6de1aef9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-108296" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e0b8b8968b650e53d35766ede2b22aa187a7301f559d1687fa6bc630c1152701.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** minimum at $x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/f7/f7abc15ac37d26d6daea9855cdebd2ef0ae5e27a27d65480b51da3cb7b19a395.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(-2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function has a global minimum at $x=1.$ The global minimum is the lowest point on the graph and our function does not have points where its value is smaller than $f(1).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/19/19d3370f7113e6ebfaa2d1f53a3d097de796e6d3413f06414d35e6a7ade9b9b6.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a5d9368-bd94-5aac-9c74-f801a63761ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a5d9368-bd94-5aac-9c74-f801a63761ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5d9368-bd94-5aac-9c74-f801a63761ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cd6d6a7c-e4ba-5e33-ad17-2e914a1c904b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58b3937e-8748-534e-8f8a-8a78179a3ca0" "answer-cd6d6a7c-e4ba-5e33-ad17-2e914a1c904b" "answer-f922dea5-ab43-5da8-94b1-11fd66e881c6" "answer-3e2ebe3b-5917-5d4e-b709-6ae7dc69f409" "answer-8b1acef0-82ab-5835-b335-a0df696d5895"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58b3937e-8748-534e-8f8a-8a78179a3ca0" :answer/id #uuid "58b3937e-8748-534e-8f8a-8a78179a3ca0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd6d6a7c-e4ba-5e33-ad17-2e914a1c904b" :answer/id #uuid "cd6d6a7c-e4ba-5e33-ad17-2e914a1c904b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f922dea5-ab43-5da8-94b1-11fd66e881c6" :answer/id #uuid "f922dea5-ab43-5da8-94b1-11fd66e881c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e2ebe3b-5917-5d4e-b709-6ae7dc69f409" :answer/id #uuid "3e2ebe3b-5917-5d4e-b709-6ae7dc69f409" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b1acef0-82ab-5835-b335-a0df696d5895" :answer/id #uuid "8b1acef0-82ab-5835-b335-a0df696d5895" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153362 :tutorial/content "A **local extremum** (or **relative extremum**) of a function is a point that is either a maximum or minimum point of the function relative to an (open) interval in the function's domain. \n\nFor example, consider the function shown in the graph below. \n\n![](images/19/197834de138cb2e05a3af391bbeec1279ad8bfddfb277b881e5e3eeb49bcb73a.png)\n\nThe graph has a peak at the point $A$ where $x=0.$ We say that the function has a **local maximum** when $x=0.$ We also say that the point $A$ is a **local maximum point** of the function. \n\nThis means that we can take an open interval of $x$-values around $x=0$ such that $A$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. \n\n![](images/d5/d522b4b0a59ff328399493bc12a770af2d99a1587b2826accb9835d7463ef9ba.png)\n\nSimilarly, the graph has a valley at the point $B$ where $x=2.$ We say that the function has a **local minimum** when $x=2.$ We can also say that the point $B$ is a **local minimum point** of the function.\n\nThis means that we can take an open interval of $x$-values around $x=2$ such that $B$ will be the lowest point on the graph in this interval. \n\n![](images/e2/e2a92d4217e1eebcc724e48cca273d2e707731ded914207e59fff149b46b4dcc.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153407 :tutorial/content "Let's go back to looking at the function $y=f(x)$ that we saw earlier.\n\n![](images/19/197834de138cb2e05a3af391bbeec1279ad8bfddfb277b881e5e3eeb49bcb73a.png)\n\nThe point $A$ where $x=0$ is a local maximum of $f(x)$ because we can draw an open interval around $x=0$ such that the point $A$ is the highest point on the graph. One such interval is $x\\in (-0.5,0.5),$ shown below:\n\n![](images/d5/d522b4b0a59ff328399493bc12a770af2d99a1587b2826accb9835d7463ef9ba.png)\n\nEverywhere in this interval, the value of the function is *less than or equal to* $f(0),$ the largest value of the function in this interval. We can write this mathematically as\n\n$\\qquad$ $f(x) \\leq f(0)$ for all $x\\in(-0.5, 0.5).$\n\nSimilarly, the point $B$ where $x=2$ is a local minimum of $f(x)$ because we can draw an open interval around $x=2$ such that the point $B$ is the lowest point on the graph. One such interval is $x\\in (1.5,2.5),$ shown below:\n\n![](images/e2/e2a92d4217e1eebcc724e48cca273d2e707731ded914207e59fff149b46b4dcc.png)\n\nEverywhere in this interval, the value of the function is *greater than or equal to* $f(2),$ the smallest value of the function in this interval. We can write this mathematically as\n\n$\\qquad$ $f(x) \\geq f(2)$ for all $x\\in(1.5, 2.5).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153406 :tutorial/content "Can a point on a graph be both a local minimum *and* a local maximum?\n\nTo answer this question, let's consider the function $f(x)$ given by the graph below. \n\n![](images/0c/0cec91d9ec8e108ee4836e816aae63722fc4c09d997790eaf283cd3e2a9c4bc6.png)\n\nNow consider the point where $x=2.$ Our goal is to determine which type of extremum it is. To do this, we consider the values of $f(x)$ in the open interval $(1.5, 2.5),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/c6/c6cf1a6237c50d5c2b651937ca46b9ae52a08dafb831d76b27ddb068d37dd501.png)\n\nNow, notice the following:\n\n- The point where $x=2$ is a local maximum because $f(x) \\le f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5)\\quad {\\color{\\green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- The point where $x=2$ is a local minimum because $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5)\\quad {\\color{\\green}\\checkmark}$\n\nTherefore, $x=2$ is both a local maximum *and* a local minimum of $f(x)!$ \n\nThis might seem strange. But, notice that $x=2$ lies within an interval where the function is constant. This is a special case where a particular point is both a local minimum and a local maximum." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152350 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186151973 :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $U.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $U$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. So, $U$ is a local maximum.\n\nA similar interval exists for the point $W,$ too. So, $W$ is also a local maximum.\n\n![](images/ac/ac0a6e28e4564883e6743b2d600cb8611723e813e85c1acb5fcc327ee3dbc9b5.png)"] [17592186152026 :question/problem "For which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y = f(x),$ shown below, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=0$\n\nII. $x=1$\n\nIII. $x=3$\n\n![](images/17/1718b48d39255b221037a439cc48d300a04c33ffb4e04c700fefb303a20ebff2.png)"] [17592186152026 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=0.$ For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/e2/e25e6e31d6ea5d7f882d4eed16c82ec8280d1ed56f275974e8f07091c0e62c5d.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(0) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-0.5,0.5).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=1.$ For any open interval containing $x=1$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(1)$.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/d1/d133d7ee4c022b47740f62b8e73ba9ea2f70e788861c25d2824b5e7236027c60.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(3) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""] [17592186152027 :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the function shown below. Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=-2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=0$\n\n![](images/9b/9b933b1b869b74f2a7340f9ba4034b970c49434d12592d3ff1e152057b6adef1.png)"] [17592186152027 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/3a/3abb7470db51fa1bdb61e15aec1739de44bf5083b7341b90a65ac93fc7f8adbb.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(-2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/71/71c6e7af0a1de77543b57d2aee242fe84295ad46c748b2f65f7cba381c47b80c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=0.$ For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/83/83de300c3e00766d46989d12b4e1708ef9a73f4d02748009a526b1646d7f0b81.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\le f(0) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-0.5,0.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] [17592186152028 :question/problem "The graph of a function $y = f(x)$ is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=0$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-2$\n\n![](images/91/91d9d4997dd58c2c3cb07efc1529487bbd9a5a2f5c611054289cfc2ba24d764c.png)"] [17592186152028 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/00/00a21a670b2080ce766ddf142eb2f37303d7af7b667e1b5038eee93879c071f7.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function does *not* have a global maximum at $x=0.$ The global maximum is the highest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is greater than $f(0).$ For example, $f(0) \\lt f(3).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/fc/fc96fe5bb938b0ca8569b864588348a4d22280e3c4a5806cdd20af6eb4bcea34.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x) \\ge f(-2) \\:$ for all $\\: x \\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""] [17592186152589 :question/problem "![](images/20/20b6e19fcb7e1fe4f33697d517c28d9563c793634cfbcd5552d842efeef3ef61.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?"] [17592186152589 :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $B.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $B$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. Hence, $B$ is a local maximum.\n\nA similar interval exists for the point $D,$ too. Hence, $D$ is also a local maximum.\n\n![](images/26/260f30379f71c006b43ec6eb26200ced27a4b40aec938140d6a4cd06910ba02c.png)"] [17592186152589 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854" :answer/id #uuid "d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854"] ["answer-d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854" :answer/value "$A,$ $C,$ and $E$ only"] [17592186150041 :answer-field/correct 17592186150042] [17592186150041 :answer-field/choices "answer-d8aa7e0f-0e11-569d-b62c-d63a9933f854"] ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/id #uuid "2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f"] ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-37221"] ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbe19cf01b4ca415802db1d505b402e2c238aad6c443170cf18cd7b79d7f238a.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the points shown are the local maxima of the function?"] ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/worked-solution "Consider the point $Q.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $Q$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. Hence, $Q$ is a local maximum.\n\n![](images/14/14d2e4c17f5a79165c2e6b1988fe949625eccb87d2880b1131705028be5884c4.png)"] ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82"] ["answer-36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121" :answer/id #uuid "36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121"] ["answer-36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121" :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only"] ["answer-69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3" :answer/id #uuid "69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3"] ["answer-69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3" :answer/value "$P$ only"] ["answer-a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a" :answer/id #uuid "a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a"] ["answer-a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a" :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only"] ["answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" :answer/id #uuid "a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703"] ["answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703" :answer/value "$Q$ only"] ["answer-abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330" :answer/id #uuid "abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330"] ["answer-abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330" :answer/value "The function does not have local maxima"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/correct "answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/choices "answer-36521294-d221-5ad2-8696-e1f86f442121"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/choices "answer-69fe4d81-06a7-5434-b1d4-340a3b5c51f3"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/choices "answer-a8b9c53e-daef-5f47-bdc8-019568ba167a"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/choices "answer-a35da3ca-b24a-5b99-9f39-e50f455e8703"] ["answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82" :answer-field/choices "answer-abeec097-a753-588f-8ea5-dd4de32b9330"] ["question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5cd7ae0b-7ec2-5c51-90c1-c5404e7bfe82"] [17592186152178 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2f37d338-5ba5-5919-bf66-41519f983a1f"] ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/id #uuid "2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab"] ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-37056"] ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d65013cac950b3e3d533dd6dfbdf1dc6582c10fcb7d80f00ab559935915d9595.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local maximum?\n\nI. $x=-1$\n\nII. $x=1$\n\nIII. $x=3$"] ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local maximum at $x=-1.$ For example, in the interval $(-1.25,-0.75),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=-1,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/a5/a5f0e23d8bed98f693ee72086b0bf17b9f65de8931bba6f16cfcc34e670a757e.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(-1)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-1.25,-0.75).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local maximum at $x=1.$ For any open interval containing $x=1,$ there will be points on the graph that lie above $f(1).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local maximum at $x=3.$ For any open interval containing $x=3,$ there will be points on the graph that lie above $f(3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/id #uuid "90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717"] ["answer-e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223" :answer/id #uuid "e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223"] ["answer-e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8" :answer/id #uuid "959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8"] ["answer-959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" :answer/id #uuid "ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c"] ["answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02" :answer/id #uuid "78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02"] ["answer-78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad" :answer/id #uuid "1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad"] ["answer-1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/correct "answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/choices "answer-e94ee3c8-4200-57dc-b3b1-c38a4cadf223"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/choices "answer-959452b5-53ec-5e51-b5b3-ddee4c8025f8"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/choices "answer-ecc307b1-edce-5714-bc4c-64086844ce1c"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/choices "answer-78dfb633-9488-5239-95f7-c6301808bf02"] ["answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717" :answer-field/choices "answer-1b806a24-f26f-55a2-80e1-991117d5b9ad"] ["question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-90e3bd18-2e16-599f-bb1b-9383fb750717"] [17592186152216 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2dea474c-b14e-5037-9ce9-358952e01aab"] ["question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/id #uuid "95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc"] ["question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-108276"] ["question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d71ebdb084e23aef4b3901aaba2e4bb4de5438fa41a3fc331bef749f3c78de76.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=-4$\n\nII. $x=-1$\n\nIII. $x=3$"] ["question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=-4.$ For any open interval containing $x=-4$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(-4).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=-1.$ For any open interval containing $x=-1$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(-1).$\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.5,3.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/bf/bfe274fe02b7200164eaad5c98aa2b19297738987f70059157d2895b989a962c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.5,3.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""] ["question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/id #uuid "73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de"] ["answer-0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd" :answer/id #uuid "0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd"] ["answer-0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480" :answer/id #uuid "274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480"] ["answer-274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224" :answer/id #uuid "6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224"] ["answer-6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434" :answer/id #uuid "4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434"] ["answer-4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a" :answer/id #uuid "8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a"] ["answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/correct "answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/choices "answer-0ff7a2f1-6a9d-58b0-9489-95fdb0edebdd"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/choices "answer-274536c7-1482-5982-a5d8-6f7cb683a480"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/choices "answer-6dffbcb2-fa18-58fe-981c-593b53989224"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/choices "answer-4fdedf1e-85b6-5c7a-b28c-1c13f89e5434"] ["answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de" :answer-field/choices "answer-8221aaeb-03bd-5c7f-bfbe-01b407418a5a"] ["question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-73e50eb5-bf95-5c3b-ba5b-752a51e4d2de"] [17592186152216 :knowledge-point/questions "question-95d717c9-1435-5503-b9b6-aa0cf5a741dc"] [17592186152594 :question/problem "![](images/c4/c46e88b9e044fccb91e0efa4ee981973a286e0335f58a70f7b1f9a856d9bfed4.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=3$\n\nII. $x=2$\n\nIII. $x=-2$"] [17592186152594 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.75,3.25),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/61/6115a87572fb93b9e3dcf69c75cd4a5efaae2dbbea90b28cb57cdd05b8db11b7.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.75,3.25).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=2.$ For any open interval containing $x=2$, there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(2).$\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/26/26acee415fa4a1038077d11f88b7c61c8b45f4aa857cc578af192e4085f7c005.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""] [17592186152594 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186150071 :answer-field/correct 17592186150075] ["question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/id #uuid "ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9"] ["question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-108273"] ["question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/problem "![](images/69/69217ab9fc86fdbb424a0716f00596197b7da9e930c74b12b82406ce2ee8354c.png)\n\nFor which of the following values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x),$ shown above, attain a local minimum?\n\nI. $x=-2$\n\nII. $x=2$\n\nIII. $x=4$"] ["question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given points in turn.\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=-2.$ For any open interval containing $x=-2,$ there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(-2).$\n\n- The function has a local minimum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/8e/8e56e79caf5c7903de977ee66894961b6068e3974ffd9ff4482b2086fad290ef.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- The function does *not* have a local minimum at $x=4.$ For any open interval containing $x=4,$ there will be points on the graph that lie below $f(4).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""] ["question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1"] ["answer-2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66" :answer/id #uuid "2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66"] ["answer-2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2" :answer/id #uuid "d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2"] ["answer-d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2" :answer/id #uuid "02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2"] ["answer-02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" :answer/id #uuid "5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab"] ["answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97" :answer/id #uuid "2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97"] ["answer-2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/correct "answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-2c8efd42-1acd-518a-acd7-fd5114b2fc66"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-d370875e-ff33-5ebf-b027-ccdba1d1d6f2"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-02383d20-0e98-5f57-be6b-6df75947ede2"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-5b537279-77cf-5ca5-9ac7-685733e882ab"] ["answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1" :answer-field/choices "answer-2f1bfff1-53da-50a6-bf4c-4a078bd1dc97"] ["question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ba3d283d-aec7-5ac6-8a37-e60669f500c1"] [17592186152216 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ea412ed1-a3cb-5bcc-876d-3ca4d60883c9"] ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/id #uuid "a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098"] ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/math-academy-id "q-108281"] ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b39c4e174ccb11a533586b57f26958a8ebfb5de0f0920a86297653471862fa7f.png)\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the function shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=-3$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=0$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=3$"] ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=-3.$ For example, in the interval $(-3.5,-2.5),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=-3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/be/be3b86690beb961d54380b72736d945af3d735410da3bfe34cfb2cdead859f81.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(-3)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-3.5,-2.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=0.$ For example, in the interval $(-0.5,0.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=0,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/43/439117bd94dbc147d3cd2de49abd45c4b4790251ce25d1a79ecb31e03081068c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(0)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-0.5,0.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=3.$ For example, in the interval $(2.75,3.25),$ the smallest value of the function is attained at $x=3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/33/33aee4724507cff3e9ca87c78aa77c0ecb0df5f59a7bcf77359c1ca4e957f73c.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(3)\\le f(x)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (2.75,3.25).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4"] ["answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" :answer/id #uuid "601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d"] ["answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548" :answer/id #uuid "caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548"] ["answer-caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce" :answer/id #uuid "fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce"] ["answer-fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358" :answer/id #uuid "527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358"] ["answer-527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3" :answer/id #uuid "2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3"] ["answer-2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/correct "answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/choices "answer-601fb171-f90d-56af-8f89-4f19d2e3bf2d"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/choices "answer-caaed8ed-6629-529d-acc1-d987c3b66548"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/choices "answer-fa2cf7e8-ae79-5fbe-b6e9-d01dfef172ce"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/choices "answer-527d4204-19b0-5174-b400-5eadfbe3a358"] ["answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e11ac1e-4cac-5e4b-be57-7818261b4df3"] ["question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0dcd1d5b-00e0-5387-8447-4e14b932e6e4"] [17592186152217 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a017d206-18fc-5343-8dce-b59fb9d7e098"] ["question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/id #uuid "50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9"] ["question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-108293"] ["question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b00882caec033394ff22a01df1f8cc417a8336b475962e73662316c3091229fa.png)\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the function given by the graph above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=-2$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a local minimum at $x=4$"] ["question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=-2.$ For example, in the interval $(-2.5,-1.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=-2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/ed/ed1ad21056cf9c05c621180126387f2e07a1cd349f151726142fb33d2b514e44.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(-2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (-2.5,-1.5).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1.$ For example, in the interval $(0.5,1.5),$ the value of the function at $x=1$ is the same as the values of the function at the other points of the interval, as shown below. \n\n![](images/ff/ff8960289497889b1fb046c05b0bb2243a8776c435bb685e3c94fb7fe832e056.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\ge f(1)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (0.5,1.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local maximum at $x=4.$ For example, in the interval $(3.75,4.25),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=4,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/b2/b2d1f1b6b065c5d3511ec02350eae1a867b9473fa2ac7c1a1cb9458d1421fe03.png)\n\nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(4)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (3.75,4.25).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] ["question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/id #uuid "a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252"] ["answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" :answer/id #uuid "813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95"] ["answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8" :answer/id #uuid "2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8"] ["answer-2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6" :answer/id #uuid "b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6"] ["answer-b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487" :answer/id #uuid "e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487"] ["answer-e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b" :answer/id #uuid "3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b"] ["answer-3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/correct "answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/choices "answer-813deb3f-953d-56d5-a179-599290773b95"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e576dfa-b2f3-54c2-a027-1f67463d58c8"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/choices "answer-b1e68446-2fd6-56de-b8a8-731047d771c6"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/choices "answer-e6872077-c939-529a-88df-fbe164e0d487"] ["answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252" :answer-field/choices "answer-3920d518-8437-576a-b180-614b1dc2ef2b"] ["question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a58b8344-1eff-5105-8f43-9022f2a12252"] [17592186152217 :knowledge-point/questions "question-50fb8efe-0b0b-50a4-80a5-fe5eb2cee4f9"] ["question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/id #uuid "e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883"] ["question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/math-academy-id "q-90634"] ["question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d13474a62324af5edcaafd10e60c6b02c257f32c015d5769512725d157e01420.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $f(x)$ attains a **global** maximum at $x=4$\n\nII. $f(x)$ attains a local maximum at $x=2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ attains a **global** minimum at $x=5$"] ["question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function does *not* have a global maximum at $x=4.$ The global maximum is the highest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is greater than $f(4).$ For example, $f(7)>f(4).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=2.$ For example, in the interval $(1.5,2.5),$ the greatest value of the function is attained at $x=2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/32/32c866706140c0bc9a40bcb0ffdca4a827578e2d16dbcefc2cdb66b5c05b1c1c.png)\n\n \nWe can write this mathematically as $f(x)\\le f(2)\\,$ for all $\\,x\\in (1.5,2.5).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function does *not* have a global minimum at $x=5.$ The global minimum is the lowest point on the graph, but our function has points where its value is smaller than $f(5).$ For example, $f(0)<f(5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""] ["question-e60840d8-8ef2-5027-842a-3130fbad5883" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-cf7eaa68-885c-514e-a7ed-820109c92b1a" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7eaa68-885c-514e-a7ed-820109c92b1a"] ["answer-f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08" :answer/id #uuid "f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08"] ["answer-f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f0731edc-4cd5-5128-a230-3aa0e3e14b08" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98" :answer/id #uuid "7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98"] ["answer-7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-7ae0b263-c07e-5e3f-ad0d-015a4284eb98" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-79e94892-8258-5ef2-824f-178abd4ba976" :answer/id #uuid "79e94892-8258-5ef2-824f-178abd4ba976"] ["answer-